#![allow(async_fn_in_trait)]
//! Strictly-typed Rust client and schema for the LXD API.
//!
//! This crate is delivered as ONE .rs file — `lxd.rs` at the crate root
//! (see `../gen_single_file.py`): the entire plugin (types, devices,
//! client, methods, dispatch, schema) in a single file, like the user's
//! emqx.rs / incus.rs. The multi-file layout in `src/` is the build
//! intermediate only. Size is irrelevant; completeness is everything.
//!
//! The client trait `LxdClient` uses native async fn in traits (stable
//! since Rust 1.75). rustc discourages this in public traits because
//! auto-trait bounds cannot be specified on the returned futures; the
//! alternative would be the `async-trait` crate, which boxes every
//! future. This crate accepts the lint and keeps the futures unboxed.
//!
//! The schema types in [`types`] are generated from LXD's `shared/api`
//! Go package (see `../gen_types.py`). They use concrete Rust types
//! throughout. Open-ended JSON payloads are modelled with
//! [`types::JsonValue`], a closed recursive enum, and raw envelope
//! metadata with `Box<serde_json::value::RawValue>`.
//!
//! `serde_json::Value` appears at the plugin dispatch boundary
//! ([`dispatch::dispatch_lxd_method`] — method name + JSON args in,
//! JSON output out) and inside the schema-document container
//! ([`state_plugin::PluginSchemaDoc`], which holds JSON Schema documents
//! — themselves JSON — for sealing). It never appears inside a schema
//! type: every Input/Output field is a concrete type.
//!
//! Every public schema type also derives `schemars::JsonSchema`, and
//! [`state_plugin::lxd_schema()`] builds the ONE sealed schema document
//! (state + all 319 methods + capabilities), written to
//! `schemas/plugin.json` — the single schema file that gets sealed into
//! the blob. Regenerate it with `cargo run --bin gen_schemas`. It is
//! self-contained (subschemas inlined, draft 2020-12). The types are the
//! single source of truth: the schema and the typed client methods both
//! derive from them.
//!
//! # Plugin pattern
//!
//! This crate follows the opdbus plugin shape: [`state_plugin::LxdState`]
//! is the single typed present-state contract, [`methods`] holds one
//! `*Input` / `*Output` pair per client method (inputs reject unknown
//! fields), [`dispatch::dispatch_lxd_method`] is the typed entry point,
//! and [`state_plugin::lxd_schema()`] builds the sealed schema document
//! (state + methods + capabilities). Devices are the typed
//! [`devices::Device`] union (`Vec<NamedDevice>` over the wire map).
//!
//! Fail closed, no drift: unknown fields are rejected, malformed input
//! fails instead of becoming a default, and anything without a typed
//! schema is left out entirely. A dispatched method returns its typed
//! Output directly — there is no acknowledgement step.
//!
//! # Quick start
//!
//! ```no_run
//! use lxd_rs::{Client, LxdClient};
//!
//! # async fn run() -> Result<(), lxd_rs::LxdError> {
//! let client = Client::new("https://127.0.0.1:8443");
//! let server = client.get_server().await?;
//! println!("LXD {} on {}", server.0.environment.server_name, server.0.environment.server_version);
//! # Ok(())
//! # }
//! ```


